{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ensembles\/gettingstarted"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Set up Ensembles to sync a Core Data or SwiftData persistent store across devices."}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble","doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/GettingStarted"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Ensembles"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ensembles synchronizes SQLite stores by recording local changes as events and exchanging them through a cloud backend. It works with both Core Data and SwiftData."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Using SwiftData?","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SwiftDataIntegration","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for a complete guide — you never need to touch Core Data directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide covers Core Data setup, starting with a complete working example using "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Develop-with-Claude-Code","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Develop with Claude Code"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/claude.com\/claude-code"},{"text":", install the Ensembles skill first. It teaches Claude the API, the cloud backends, Ensembles 2 → 3 migration, the seed policy, and the common pitfalls, so it writes correct setup code and diagnoses sync issues without hand-holding:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["\/plugin marketplace add mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3","\/plugin install ensembles@ensembles"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Add Ensembles to Your Project","anchor":"Add-Ensembles-to-Your-Project","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the Ensembles package to your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":" or via Xcode’s package dependencies:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["https:\/\/github.com\/mentalfaculty\/Ensembles3.git"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Import the core module and one cloud backend:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit   \/\/ or EnsemblesLocalFile, EnsemblesMemory"]},{"anchor":"Complete-Example-Core-Data-with-CloudKit","level":2,"text":"Complete Example: Core Data with CloudKit","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here’s a complete, working setup for a SwiftUI app that syncs via CloudKit. This uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer"},{"text":", which creates the Core Data stack for you and syncs automatically.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"1-Create-Your-Core-Data-Model","level":3,"text":"1. Create Your Core Data Model","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In Xcode, add a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".xcdatamodeld"},{"text":" file to your project (e.g., ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Model.xcdatamodeld"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"). Define your entities as usual. For this example, we’ll assume a "},{"code":"Note","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uniqueID"},{"type":"text","text":" (String) attributes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"2-Define-Your-Model-with-Syncable","level":3,"text":"2. Define Your Model with `Syncable`"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For deduplication, conform your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"text":" subclass to the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" protocol and specify which property holds the global identifier. A UUID assigned at creation time is usually the best choice:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import CoreData","import Ensembles","","class Note: NSManagedObject, Syncable {","    static let globalIdentifierKey = \"uniqueID\"","    @NSManaged var uniqueID: String","    @NSManaged var title: String","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A global identifier ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"must never change"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" once it has been assigned. Changing it after sync has begun will cause duplicates or data loss.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a fixed, meaningful value instead of a UUID for singleton objects or reference data like tags, where two devices might independently create the same logical object.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"3. Set Up the Container","level":3,"anchor":"3-Set-Up-the-Container","type":"heading"},{"code":["import SwiftUI","import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","@main","struct MyApp: App {","    let syncContainer: CoreDataEnsembleContainer","","    init() {","        \/\/ The model URL points to the .momd bundle compiled from your .xcdatamodeld","        let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","        \/\/ This creates a full Core Data stack automatically:","        \/\/ - SQLite store at Application Support\/MyNotes.sqlite","        \/\/ - Main-queue viewContext for your UI","        \/\/ - Auto-sync on save, on app activation, and on a 5-minute timer","        let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","            name: \"MyNotes\",","            modelURL: modelURL,","            cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","                privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","                schemaVersion: .v2","            )","        )!","","        self.syncContainer = container","    }","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","                .environment(","                    \\.managedObjectContext,","                    syncContainer.viewContext","                )","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That’s the complete setup. The container discovers "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" conformances automatically, attaches to the cloud, and begins syncing. Remote changes are merged into ","type":"text"},{"code":"viewContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so your UI stays up to date.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Respond to Events (Optional)","level":3,"anchor":"4-Respond-to-Events-Optional","type":"heading"},{"code":["\/\/ Called after remote changes are merged into viewContext","container.didSaveMergeChanges = { notification in","    print(\"Merged remote changes\")","}","","\/\/ Called if a sync fails","container.didEncounterError = { error in","    print(\"Sync error: \\(error)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Using-a-Custom-Store-Location","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Using a Custom Store Location"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need control over where the SQLite file lives, pass an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"storeURL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let appSupport = FileManager.default.urls(","    for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask",").first!","let storeURL = appSupport.appendingPathComponent(\"MyApp\/data.sqlite\")","try FileManager.default.createDirectory(","    at: storeURL.deletingLastPathComponent(),","    withIntermediateDirectories: true",")","","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    storeURL: storeURL,","    modelURL: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")!"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Working-with-an-Existing-Core-Data-Stack","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Working with an Existing Core Data Stack"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you already have an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSPersistentContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", pass it in directly:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    persistentContainer: myPersistentContainer,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Or if you have an existing ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSManagedObjectContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    viewContext: myContext,","    persistentStoreURL: myStoreURL,","    managedObjectModel: myContext.persistentStoreCoordinator!.managedObjectModel,","    managedObjectModels: nil,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Auto-Sync-Configuration","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Auto-Sync Configuration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Control when syncing occurs with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AutoSyncPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    autoSyncPolicy: [.onSave, .onTimer],   \/\/ Sync on save and timer, not on activation","    timerInterval: 30                       \/\/ Timer fires every 30 seconds",")","let container = CoreDataEnsembleContainer(","    name: \"MyNotes\",","    modelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: cloudFS,","    configuration: config",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"autoSyncPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".manual"},{"text":" and call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer\/sync()"},{"text":" yourself for full control over timing.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Backward-Compatibility-with-Ensembles-2","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Backward Compatibility with Ensembles 2"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re transitioning from Ensembles 2 and some users may still be on E2, set the compatibility mode:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let config = EnsembleContainerConfiguration(","    compatibilityMode: .ensembles2Compatible",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This restricts exports to formats that Ensembles 2 peers can parse. Switch to ","type":"text"},{"code":".ensembles3","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the default) once all users have upgraded.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"The-Manual-Way-CoreDataEnsemble","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The Manual Way: CoreDataEnsemble"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For more control over the sync lifecycle, use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly. This is useful when you need to manage attach\/detach timing, handle specific delegate methods, or integrate with a complex Core Data stack.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Create-and-Attach","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Create and Attach"},{"code":["import Ensembles","import EnsemblesCloudKit","","\/\/ Get the store URL from your persistent store coordinator","let store = persistentStoreCoordinator.persistentStores.first!","let storeURL = store.url!","let modelURL = Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"Model\", withExtension: \"momd\")!","","let ensemble = CoreDataEnsemble(","    ensembleIdentifier: \"MyNotes\",","    persistentStoreURL: storeURL,","    managedObjectModelURL: modelURL,","    cloudFileSystem: CloudKitFileSystem(","        privateDatabaseForUbiquityContainerIdentifier: \"iCloud.com.example.mynotes\",","        schemaVersion: .v2","    )",")","ensemble?.delegate = self","","\/\/ Attach registers this device in the cloud","try await ensemble?.attachPersistentStore()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/ensembleIdentifier"},{"text":" must be the same on all devices that should sync together. If you have multiple persistent stores, create one ensemble per store with a unique identifier.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Avoid saving to the persistent store while attaching. If a save is detected, attachment will fail with an error and you will need to retry.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"anchor":"Sync-Changes","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Changes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/sync(options:)"},{"text":" periodically — for example, when the app enters the foreground, on a timer, or in response to a push notification:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["try await ensemble?.sync()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sync downloads remote events, replays them into the local store, and uploads new local events. Sync errors are usually transient — just retry later.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Handle-the-Delegate","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Handle the Delegate"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Implement ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleDelegate"},{"text":" to respond to sync events. The most important method merges remote changes into your main context:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["extension AppDelegate: CoreDataEnsembleDelegate {","    func coreDataEnsemble(","        _ ensemble: CoreDataEnsemble,","        didSaveMergeChangesWith notification: Notification","    ) {","        viewContext.perform {","            self.viewContext.mergeChanges(fromContextDidSave: notification)","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSManagedObject"},{"text":" subclasses conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/Syncable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", you don’t need to implement ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"globalIdentifiersForManagedObjects"},{"text":" — the ensemble discovers identifier properties automatically. You only need the delegate method if you use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CoreDataEnsemble"},{"text":" directly without ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsembleContainer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Other delegate methods let you:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inspect and repair merge data"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" before it’s committed ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shouldSaveMergedChangesIn:reparationContext:"},{"type":"text","text":")"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Handle save failures"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" during merging (","type":"text"},{"code":"didFailToSaveMergedChangesIn:error:reparationContext:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"React to forced detaches"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" caused by identity changes or data corruption (","type":"text"},{"code":"didDetachWithError:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/ConflictResolution"},{"text":" for more on conflict handling and the reparation context.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Detach","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Detach"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To stop syncing, detach from the cloud:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["try await ensemble?.detachPersistentStore()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This removes local sync data (event logs and metadata). The persistent store itself is not affected. You can re-attach later to resume syncing.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Seed-Policies","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Seed Policies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy"},{"text":" parameter controls how existing data in the store is handled during attachment:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/mergeAllData","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (default) — Imports local data so it can be merged with data from other devices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy\/excludeLocalData","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — Ignores local data. Use this when you want to start fresh from cloud data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Sync-Options","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Sync Options"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For advanced control, pass ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncOptions"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Download only — don't integrate or upload","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .cloudFileRetrievalOnly)","","\/\/ Force a rebase to compact sync history","try await ensemble?.sync(options: .forceRebase)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Process-Pending-Changes","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Process Pending Changes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iOS, the app may be suspended before Ensembles finishes recording a save. Call ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/processPendingChanges()"},{"text":" — for example, in a background task — to ensure all changes are fully stored:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["try await ensemble?.processPendingChanges()"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Monitor-Activity","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Monitor Activity"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Track long-running operations via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/currentActivity"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/CoreDataEnsemble\/activityProgress"},{"text":", or observe these notifications:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleDidBeginActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — An activity started","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleDidMakeProgressWithActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — Progress updated (includes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SyncingPhase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/AttachingPhase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"coreDataEnsembleWillEndActivity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — An activity finished (may include an error)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Ensembles/documentation/Ensembles/SeedPolicy":{"kind":"symbol","title":"SeedPolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/Ensembles\/documentation\/Ensembles\/SeedPolicy","abstract":[{"text":"Controls how existing data in the persistent store is treated when a